preferred platform. It was just after 8.30am on Wednesday March 13 1996 when a team of eight detectives were called to a residence in the New South Wales suburb of Valby and Park Rail. were called to a residence in the New South Wales suburb of Alpion Park Rail. Detective Sergeant Danny Sharkey, who headed the crew, quickly drove to the address in Sheewater Boulevard, accompanied by several colleagues. The house was easy to spot, thanks to an ambulance parked outside. As the detectives pulled up to the small one-story brick home, they saw a tall, dark-haired teenager doubled up on the front lawn with an older man next to him. The teenager was crying and asking repeatedly, what's happened? Who's done this?
